<!-- Shuffle-ON glyph for the full-screen player ONLY, and it is the PLAIN arrows on purpose.
     ic_shuffle_on_40dp - the one this replaces here - is the same arrows wrapped in a full
     rounded-square OUTLINE, i.e. it carries the on-state as a container of its own. Once the button
     has a filled tonal circle behind it (drawable/bg_player_transport_circle.xml) that outline sits
     inside a filled circle and reads as two nested containers, so the container state moves to the
     circle and the glyph goes back to plain.
     ⚠️ THIS IS A NEW FILE INSTEAD OF AN EDIT TO ic_shuffle_on_40dp BECAUSE THAT DRAWABLE IS
     SHIPPED OFF-DEVICE. PlayerCommands.getShuffleButton passes it to
     CommandButton.setCustomIconResId, which is what Android Auto head units and the media
     notification render. Editing it would change the car icon as a side effect of an in-app styling
     pass - the kind of change that only shows up on a head unit. Same reason anim_shuffle is left
     alone and anim_shuffle_plain.xml exists: anim_shuffle is also used by fragment_player_tv.xml.
     Geometry is copied from ic_shuffle_40dp unchanged - 28dp at a 960 viewport - because the OFF and
     ON glyphs must be the same optical size, and because the layout note at trackShuffle records
     that shuffle's 28dp intrinsic has to stay equal to trackRepeat's app:iconSize of 28dp.
     ⚠️ CONSEQUENCE WORTH KNOWING: with the arrows identical in both states, shuffle's state is
     carried by the FILL ALONE. Repeat still has two channels (slash OFF / plain ALL / "1" ONE); this
     one does not. That is the agreed design for a binary control, not an oversight - if it ever needs
     a second channel, this file is where the differing glyph goes, and nothing outside the phone
     player reads it. -->
